+              use it. Inspect the pivot, rotor anchors or frame regions when the slot needs them.
+            </li>
+            <li data-studio-host="body">
+              <strong>Validate and stage.</strong> Choose Validate and stage replacement. Fix any
+              reported requirement and try again. Preparation alone has not added the replacement to
+              your workspace; staging creates the draft revision.
+            </li>
+            <li data-studio-host="body">
+              <strong>Inspect, save and export.</strong> Check the comparison and applicable
+              previews. Save local revision keeps the workspace on this device. Export .rltheme
+              transfers the staged collection, original files and revision history for review and
+              release adoption. Neither action publishes the public game or changes player saves.
+            </li>
+          </ol>
+          <h3 data-studio-host="heading">Keep your work</h3>
+          <p data-studio-host="body">
+            Pixel Undo and Redo affect the sprite editor. Undo draft and Redo draft affect staged,
+            unsaved workspace revisions. A successful Save local revision clears the draft undo
+            stack. Prepare and stage an unfinished sprite or upload, or explicitly discard it,
+            before saving, exporting or switching assets.
+          </p>
+          <p data-studio-host="body">
+            If local saving is unavailable, finish and stage any pending edit, then export your
+            workspace. Keep that export before Reset to saved, which discards staged unsaved
+            changes. Reload saved requires you to resolve unfinished edits and staged changes first.
+            A stale save from another tab also needs this recovery path.
+          </p>
+          <p data-studio-host="body">
+            Import collection validates a .rltheme bundle and stages its assets for inspection. It
+            does not save or publish them. Use Undo draft to reverse the import before saving, or
+            Save local revision when you want to keep it on this device.
+          </p>
+          <h3 data-studio-host="heading">Review what the preview can show</h3>
+          <p data-studio-host="body">
+            Native pixels, enlarged pixels, transparency and field context help inspect an asset.
+            These are bounded previews, not a complete playthrough of every mode or screen.
+            Technical validation does not approve the art: record the checks you actually performed
+            before marking a revision reviewed.
+          </p>
+          <p data-studio-host="body">
+            Interface changes text face, size and reduced effects for the tools without staging a
+            theme change. Opening or closing this guide leaves preview playback as you chose it.
+            Press Escape while reading here to close the guide; Escape outside it keeps the normal
+            operation and editor behavior.
+          </p>
+          <button id="studio-guide-close" data-studio-host="control" type="button" hidden>
+            Close guide
+          </button>
+        </div>
+      </details>
